// A seam ends every borrow (actor-continuations, the seam's step 1). It is a
// scope ending, not a prohibition: a borrow held across an 'await' is refused
// only where it is named after it, and then by the ordinary diagnostic for a
// borrow that is no longer valid, ErrorFrozen, pointing at the 'await' as
// where the borrow ended.
//
// - a borrow of the actor's state through 'self', and one of a local, used
//   after the seam;
// - a borrow held by a droppable whose finalizer reads it: its death, after
//   the seam, uses it;
// - a borrow a value carries, made before the seam for a call made after it:
//   'peek(v, await give())', 'v' a local holding a borrow. A value written to
//   the left of the 'await' is made before the seam and travels; the borrow
//   it carries ends there.
//
// A borrow of a plain path written to the left of the 'await' for a call made
// after it -- 'take(&x, await give())', or 'self' lent as a method's receiver
// -- is no such borrow: the rest of the statement runs after the seam, and the
// borrow is taken there (concurrency_await_expr). One a call made is refused,
// ErrorAwaitLeftCall (concurrency_await_expr_refused).
//
// A borrow a caller lends through a parameter never reaches a seam: a
// behaviour's parameters cross to the actor's thread, so none is a borrow, and
// a synchronous 'fn', which may take one, holds no 'await'
// (concurrency_await_place).
//
// The same borrow not named after the seam is no error of the seam's: the
// 'await' is refused for what it awaits alone (ErrorAwaitNotFuture), the
// borrow among those its seam would end. 'self' is lent afresh after the seam,
// so it is named there freely. Each 'await' is on a plain function, which
// waits for no answer, so that the seam's rules are what the file pins.

mod concurrency_await_borrow;

import actors;

struct Holds {
  pub r &u64;
  fn final(self &uni) {imm seen = *r;}
}

struct View {
  pub r &u64;
}

fn give() u64 {5u64;}
fn take(r &u64, n u64) u64 {*r + n;}
fn peek(v View, n u64) u64 {*v.r + n;}

actor Page {
  body u64;

  pub async do ofState(self) {
    imm r = &body;
    await give();          //~ ErrorFrozen "The borrow 'r' holds of '*self' (made at 54:13) ends at this 'await'"
    body = *r;
  }

  pub async do ofLocal(self) {
    imm x = 3u64;
    imm r = &x;
    await give();          //~ ErrorFrozen "The borrow 'r' holds of 'x' (made at 61:13) ends at this 'await'"
    body = *r;
  }

  pub async do finalized(self) {
    imm x = 3u64;
    imm h = new Holds(&x);
    await give();          //~ ErrorFrozen "and 'h' is used again when 'h''s value is finalized"
  }

  pub async do inFlight(self) {
    imm x = 3u64;
    imm v = new View(&x);
    body = peek(v, await give());    //~ ErrorFrozen "A borrow of 'x' (made at 74:22) ends at this 'await'"
  }

  pub async do takenAfter(self) {
    imm x = 3u64;
    body = take(&x, await give());   //~ ErrorAwaitNotFuture "move into the continuation's record [x]"
  }

  pub async do receiver(self) {
    body = self.twice(await give()); //~ ErrorAwaitNotFuture "move into the continuation's record []"
  }

  fn twice(self, n u64) u64 {n + n;}

  pub async do notNamed(self) {
    imm r = &body;
    body = *r + 1u64;
    await give();          //~ ErrorAwaitNotFuture "end the borrows held by [r]"
    body = body + 1u64;
  }
}
